WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.315
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.615 --> 00:00:08.932
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.232 --> 00:00:14.613
Unit eighteen: So / Neither. Today you will agree with what other people say.

4
00:00:14.913 --> 00:00:17.588
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:21.824
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.683 --> 00:00:23.824
So am I.

7
00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:27.048
So am I means I also am the same.

8
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.896
I am tired. So am I.

9
00:00:30.483 --> 00:00:33.020
Your turn. Say: So am I.

10
00:00:35.867 --> 00:00:37.088
So am I.

11
00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:39.048
Neither do I.

12
00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:42.398
Neither do I means I also do not.

13
00:00:42.983 --> 00:00:45.543
I don't like fish. Neither do I.

14
00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.559
Your turn. Say: Neither do I.

15
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.691
Neither do I.

16
00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:54.381
Agreement.

17
00:00:55.383 --> 00:00:58.045
Agreement means when people have the same opinion.

18
00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:00.057
We reached an agreement.

19
00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:03.128
Your turn. Say: Agreement.

20
00:01:05.967 --> 00:01:07.072
Agreement.

21
00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:08.771
Also.

22
00:01:09.783 --> 00:01:11.783
Also means in addition; too.

23
00:01:12.383 --> 00:01:13.849
I also like music.

24
00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:16.975
Your turn. Say: Also.

25
00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:20.730
Also.

26
00:01:21.483 --> 00:01:22.508
Me too.

27
00:01:23.517 --> 00:01:27.049
Me too means an informal way to agree with a positive statement.

28
00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:29.989
I love football. Me too!

29
00:01:30.583 --> 00:01:33.270
Your turn. Say: Me too.

30
00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:37.088
Me too.

31
00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:39.025
Me neither.

32
00:01:40.017 --> 00:01:43.793
Me neither means an informal way to agree with a negative statement.

33
00:01:44.383 --> 00:01:46.455
I can't swim. Me neither.

34
00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:49.412
Your turn. Say: Me neither.

35
00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:53.314
Me neither.

36
00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.469
Positive agreement.

37
00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:59.563
Positive agreement means agreeing with a positive statement.

38
00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.138
So do I is positive agreement.

39
00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:05.716
Your turn. Say: Positive agreement.

40
00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:10.079
Positive agreement.

41
00:02:10.817 --> 00:02:12.131
Negative agreement.

42
00:02:13.117 --> 00:02:16.057
Negative agreement means agreeing with a negative statement.

43
00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.650
Neither do I is negative agreement.

44
00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:22.773
Your turn. Say: Negative agreement.

45
00:02:25.633 --> 00:02:26.971
Negative agreement.

46
00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:31.255
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:32.117 --> 00:02:35.744
Visal, I am tired today. How can you agree with me?

48
00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:47.962
So am I. We use so + helping verb + subject to agree with a positive statement: I like tea. So do I. She can swim. So can he.

49
00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:50.678
And with a negative statement?

50
00:02:51.783 --> 00:03:04.068
We use neither + helping verb + subject: I don't like fish. Neither do I. He can't drive. Neither can she. We can also say Me too or Me neither in informal speech.

51
00:03:05.183 --> 00:03:07.078
Which helping verb do I choose?

52
00:03:08.183 --> 00:03:20.617
The same as in the first sentence. Am becomes am, do becomes do, can becomes can. If the sentence has no helping verb, use do, does or did: I went. So did I.

53
00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:23.580
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:24.417 --> 00:03:28.204
Grammar focus: So and neither plus helping verb plus subject.

55
00:03:28.504 --> 00:03:29.714
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:30.417 --> 00:03:32.651
I am tired. So am I.

57
00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:36.307
I don't like fish. Neither do I.

58
00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:39.521
She can swim. So can he.

59
00:03:40.467 --> 00:03:49.760
Use so + helping verb + subject to agree with a positive statement and neither + helping verb + subject for a negative one. Use the same helping verb.

60
00:03:50.517 --> 00:03:54.785
Be careful! Don't say: I like tea. So I do.

61
00:03:56.733 --> 00:03:59.734
Say: I like tea. So do I.

62
00:04:00.034 --> 00:04:02.196
Put the helping verb before the subject.

63
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.583
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:07.217
Me Too.

65
00:04:07.517 --> 00:04:09.658
I am hungry. So am I.

66
00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:13.621
I don't like spicy food. Neither do I.

67
00:04:14.633 --> 00:04:16.844
She can swim. So can her brother.

68
00:04:17.833 --> 00:04:20.335
He hasn't finished. Neither have we.

69
00:04:21.333 --> 00:04:24.215
Me too and me neither are informal, but they mean the same.

70
00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:29.232
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:30.083 --> 00:04:32.840
I like pizza. So blank I.

72
00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:36.190
A, am. B, do. C, does.

73
00:04:39.733 --> 00:04:41.338
The answer is B: do.

74
00:04:42.483 --> 00:04:44.938
I can't swim. Neither blank I.

75
00:04:45.238 --> 00:04:48.590
A, do. B, can. C, am.

76
00:04:52.133 --> 00:04:53.808
The answer is B: can.

77
00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:57.347
She is late. So blank he.

78
00:04:57.647 --> 00:05:00.627
A, is. B, does. C, do.

79
00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:05.655
The answer is A: is.

80
00:05:06.817 --> 00:05:08.398
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:08.698 --> 00:05:12.863
A, Neither I do.. B, Neither do I.. C, So I do..

82
00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.783
The answer is B: Neither do I..

83
00:05:19.917 --> 00:05:22.555
According to the reading, which phrase is informal?

84
00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:27.031
A, Me too. B, So am I. C, Neither do I.

85
00:05:30.567 --> 00:05:32.694
The answer is A: Me too.

86
00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:37.365
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:38.217 --> 00:05:41.389
Practice agreeing with a partner's sentence using 'so' or 'neither'.

88
00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:51.649
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:51.949 --> 00:06:05.697
My partner says: I love music. I answer: So do I. Then my partner says: I don't like loud noise. I answer: Neither do I. I use the same helping verb as my partner.

90
00:06:05.997 --> 00:06:07.625
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:08.517 --> 00:06:14.269
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and so and neither plus helping verb plus subject.

92
00:06:14.569 --> 00:06:18.150
Today's value is empathy. Think about how others feel.

93
00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:21.114
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:21.414 --> 00:06:23.822
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

